============================================================
17. FIRECRAWL PROVENANCE MUST BE VISIBLE
============================================================

If Firecrawl is used to discover information, this MUST be represented in provenance.

Do not hide the use of Firecrawl.

Separate:

1. SOURCE
   The actual article/site containing the information.

2. DISCOVERY METHOD
   How our system found it.

Example:

Source:
Football Tribe

Published:
2026-09-04

Claim:
Contract reportedly runs until December 2026

Status:
Reported

Discovered via:
Firecrawl web search

Source URL:
[original article URL]

This distinction is important because Firecrawl is a discovery/extraction service, not itself the authority for the claim.

============================================================
18. DO NOT MAKE FIRECRAWL THE SOURCE OF TRUTH
============================================================

The system must never reason:

"Firecrawl found it, therefore it is true."

Instead:

Firecrawl
  -> finds candidate source
  -> retrieves source content
  -> source is evaluated
  -> relevant claim extracted
  -> provenance retained
  -> confidence/verification status assigned

Prefer primary sources where available:

- official club
- official league
- official competition
- player interview
- official announcement

Then reputable journalism.

Do not treat rumours as facts.

============================================================
19. LLM USAGE
============================================================

LLM use is optional and must solve a concrete problem.

Do NOT add a visible "AI assistant" merely for marketing.

The most useful LLM roles are:

1. classify whether an article is relevant to a former player
2. extract structured claims
3. distinguish contract/transfer/loan/etc.
4. identify duplicate coverage of the same event
5. summarise multiple verified articles into a compact watchlist item
6. distinguish confirmed/report/rumour where evidence allows

The LLM must NOT invent facts.

Every extracted claim must retain source provenance.

Prefer structured JSON output.

Conceptual example:

{
  "player": "Samuel Gustafson",
  "topic": "contract",
  "claim": "Contract reportedly runs until December 2026",
  "status": "reported",
  "source": "Football Tribe",
  "sourceUrl": "...",
  "publishedAt": "...",
  "discoveredVia": "firecrawl",
  "evidenceType": "reported_media"
}

============================================================
